# Numra book — Cloudflare Pages security headers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSP is authoritative here (Astro's experimental security.csp
# meta-tag emitter is disabled).
#
# style-src 'unsafe-inline' is REQUIRED for the book because:
#   - KaTeX emits per-glyph inline `style="height:0.84em;..."` and
#     `style="vertical-align:..."` attributes for math layout. Each
#     value is unique per equation, so hash-based CSP cannot cover
#     them (would need 'unsafe-hashes' + a hash per attribute value).
#   - Pagefind's search UI uses inline styles for the dropdown
#     chrome and result-snippet highlighting.
#   - Starlight components emit scoped inline <style> blocks.
#
# This is the standard Starlight + KaTeX deployment posture. The
# trade-off is acceptable: script-src remains strict, the book has
# no user-generated content, and CSS-injection attacks against a
# static docs site have minimal attack surface.
#
# font-src 'self' data:: data: covers the few inline-decoded glyphs
# Astro/Starlight emits (Inter Variable subsetting strategy).
#
# script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline': Starlight injects many inline
# <script> blocks for the theme switcher, mobile menu, sidebar
# scrollspy, search trigger, and table-of-contents behavior — all
# page-specific so a static hash list cannot cover them. Pagefind's
# UI also bootstraps via inline scripts. Without 'unsafe-inline':
# theme toggle is dead, search hangs at "Searching for…", mobile
# nav doesn't open. This is the documented Starlight + Pagefind
# deployment posture.
#
# The trade-off: docs site has zero user-generated content paths,
# all inline scripts are framework-controlled. The protection comes
# from `'self'` (no third-party JS except CF beacon), `frame-ancestors
# 'none'`, COOP/CORP, X-Frame-Options DENY.
#
# worker-src 'self' blob:: Pagefind spawns a Web Worker from a Blob
# URL for indexed search; without `blob:` the worker is blocked and
# search hangs.
#
# 'unsafe-eval' + 'wasm-unsafe-eval' in script-src: Pagefind
# instantiates a WebAssembly module inside a Web Worker that
# powers search. Pagefind's hosting docs claim 'wasm-unsafe-eval'
# alone is sufficient in browsers shipping the keyword since 2022,
# but in practice the worker context in Firefox (and some Chrome
# builds) still trips a CompileError on WebAssembly.instantiate()
# when only 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is set. Adding the broader
# 'unsafe-eval' keyword as a paired fallback resolves the
# block in all cases. This is a Pagefind / WebAssembly-in-worker
# quirk; the marketing site does not need either keyword (no
# search, no WASM).
#
# Reference: https://pagefind.app/docs/hosting/ — recommends
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; field experience shows 'unsafe-eval' is
# the universal fallback when the modern keyword alone fails.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; worker-src 'self' blob:; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off

# Long-cache fingerprinted assets
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
